# OKMate

OKMate is an open-source tool for Open Knowledge Format (OKF) knowledge.
Humans and agents read and write the same git-owned Markdown.

:card-grid.begin
    :link-card[page: "docs/install", title: "Install", summary: "Homebrew cask, cargo, the macOS app zip, and how the app updates."]
    :link-card[page: "docs/index", title: "Docs", summary: "Human manual: first bundle, git ownership, multiple roots, CLI, and desktop."]
    :link-card[page: "agents/index", title: "Agents", summary: "Fetch /llms.txt, install the CLI and skill, then work one root at a time."]
    :link-card[href: "https://github.com/koliyo/okmate", title: "GitHub", summary: "Source, releases, and issues."]
:card-grid.end

## Four claims

- **Open source.** The CLI, desktop preview, and OKF engine live in [github.com/koliyo/okmate](https://github.com/koliyo/okmate).
- **OKF compatible.** Bundles are inert Markdown plus YAML. `okmate` checks, inspects, searches, and builds them; it does not compile Rocdown.
- **Git ownership.** Directory roots are writable. Git roots are read-only snapshots. Tokens never appear in `roots` JSON.
- **Multiple bundles.** Several knowledge trees stay coordinated without merging catalogs. List roots, then run `check`, `inspect`, `search`, or `build` on one path.
